  "strategy": "Kithkin go-wide with a Mirrormind Crown copy-engine ceiling",
  "colors": "GW",
  "identity": "A GW Kithkin go-wide deck with a Mirrormind Crown copy-engine CEILING. When the Crown is attached to Champion of the Clachan, the first token event each turn becomes copies of a 4/5 Kithkin lord, and because each copy carries the static 'Other Kithkin you control get +1/+1' the copies pump each other and the whole token board -- quadratic damage off a linear token engine. Clachan Festival's two-token ETB converts one redirect into TWO copies. That is the ceiling, not the plan: the full assembly needs two singletons and lands in roughly 9-12% of games (see crown_singleton_ledger). The other ~88% is a Kithkin go-wide deck that kills with an anthem stack -- Champion, Kinbinding and Gallant Fowlknight x2 -- over a board fed by 8 token producers.",
